WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.267
The Bird and the Whale

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:08.109
(An original tale by TheFableCottage.com)

00:00:09.749 --> 00:00:13.549
Once there was a bird 
who fell in love with a whale.

00:00:13.869 --> 00:00:17.536
And a whale who fell in love with a bird.

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:22.081
The bird loved the whale's beautiful smile.

00:00:22.481 --> 00:00:26.651
He loved the way she swam through 
the water so gracefully.

00:00:27.331 --> 00:00:31.052
The whale loved the bird's handsome 
white feathers.

00:00:31.452 --> 00:00:34.866
She loved to watch him soar 
through the sky.

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:40.357
And they both loved to eat 
lots of tiny fish.

00:00:43.747 --> 00:00:47.536
All summer, the bird and the whale 
met in the bay.

00:00:47.909 --> 00:00:50.256
They talked and talked.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:53.588
They talked about the moon, 
and the tides, 

00:00:53.588 --> 00:00:55.317
and the ships on the ocean.

00:00:56.318 --> 00:00:59.572
The bird told jokes and made 
the whale laugh.

00:01:00.444 --> 00:01:04.667
The whale sang beautiful songs 
that made the bird cry

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.467
(even though he didn't know why).

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:13.296
"One day, you could meet my family in the ocean," said the whale.

00:01:13.917 --> 00:01:18.478
"And you could meet my friends 
on the land," said the bird.

00:01:18.936 --> 00:01:21.136
Everything was perfect.

00:01:21.787 --> 00:01:27.392
But the world does not stop turning 
just because a bird and whale fall in love. 

00:01:27.865 --> 00:01:30.005
 Summer turned into autumn,

00:01:30.172 --> 00:01:32.319
and autumn turned into winter.

00:01:32.933 --> 00:01:34.933
The ocean turned cold,

00:01:35.173 --> 00:01:39.054
and all the other whales left 
for warmer waters.

00:01:39.601 --> 00:01:44.254
"Come with me to warmer waters," 
said the whale.

00:01:44.573 --> 00:01:47.061
"It’s a wonderful place.

00:01:47.061 --> 00:01:52.302
It's always warm, and there are 
so many fish to eat."

00:01:53.162 --> 00:01:56.390
"I love to eat fish," said the bird. 

00:01:56.473 --> 00:01:58.648
"And I love you. 

00:01:58.717 --> 00:02:00.938
I will follow you anywhere.

00:02:01.577 --> 00:02:04.416
But first, teach me to be a whale?"

00:02:05.096 --> 00:02:09.579
"Like this!" said the whale, "follow me!"

00:02:09.821 --> 00:02:12.673
and she dived deep into the water.

00:02:13.297 --> 00:02:15.537
"OK!" said the bird,

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:18.754
and he also dived deep into the water.

00:02:19.154 --> 00:02:21.761
Deeper and deeper he went.

00:02:22.969 --> 00:02:27.894
"I'm swimming!" he laughed.  "I'm a whale!"

00:02:28.255 --> 00:02:30.833
But soon he couldn't breathe. 

00:02:30.893 --> 00:02:33.521
He returned to the surface, gasping.

00:02:34.234 --> 00:02:37.230
He tried and tried and tried again,

00:02:38.062 --> 00:02:40.721
but he ran out of breath every time.

00:02:41.217 --> 00:02:45.231
"I don't think a bird can become a whale," said the bird.

00:02:45.649 --> 00:02:47.336
"Come with me instead!

00:02:47.336 --> 00:02:49.439
I live up on the cliffs.

00:02:49.564 --> 00:02:51.564
It's a wonderful place. 

00:02:51.564 --> 00:02:53.484
It's warm and cosy, 

00:02:53.692 --> 00:02:57.000
and every morning you can 
watch the sun rise."

00:02:57.414 --> 00:03:01.436
"I love to watch the sun rise," said the whale.

00:03:01.677 --> 00:03:05.928
"And I love you. I will follow you anywhere.

00:03:05.928 --> 00:03:08.875
But first, teach me to be a bird?"

00:03:09.125 --> 00:03:13.076
"Like this!" said the bird. "Follow me!"

00:03:13.215 --> 00:03:17.149
and he flapped his wings 
and soared into the sky.

00:03:17.477 --> 00:03:19.890
"OK!" said the whale.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:25.532
She squeezed her eyes shut 
and flapped her fins, just like the bird.

00:03:25.619 --> 00:03:28.487
She flapped and flapped, up and down. 

00:03:28.709 --> 00:03:31.664
Water splashed everywhere!

00:03:32.656 --> 00:03:37.320
"I'm flying!" she laughed. 
"I'm a bird!"  

00:03:37.653 --> 00:03:42.111
But when she opened her eyes, 
she wasn't soaring in the sky.

00:03:42.227 --> 00:03:44.227
She was still in the water.

00:03:45.087 --> 00:03:48.166
She tried and tried and tried again, 

00:03:48.388 --> 00:03:50.708
but she could not fly.

00:03:51.109 --> 00:03:55.670
"I don't think a whale can become a bird," 
said the whale.

00:03:55.967 --> 00:04:03.058
"But if you can't fly, and I can't swim, 
where can we live together?" said the bird.

00:04:03.457 --> 00:04:08.355
"We will stay here — in the waves!" 
said the whale.

00:04:08.566 --> 00:04:11.290
But the bird shook his head sadly.

00:04:11.794 --> 00:04:15.515
"You love to swim deep in the ocean," he said. 

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:18.127
That is your favourite thing to do.

00:04:18.447 --> 00:04:20.586
You would never be happy here."

00:04:21.597 --> 00:04:23.424
The whale sighed.

00:04:23.692 --> 00:04:28.280
"And you love to fly and soar into the sky," she said.

00:04:28.489 --> 00:04:31.116
"That is your favourite thing to do.

00:04:31.302 --> 00:04:34.296
You would never be happy here either."

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:39.662
And so, because the bird and whale loved each other so much,

00:04:39.801 --> 00:04:41.371
they said goodbye.

00:04:42.624 --> 00:04:44.606
But they never forgot each other.

00:04:45.555 --> 00:04:50.081
Every time the whale saw a bird flying high in the sky,

00:04:50.311 --> 00:04:52.458
she thought of her bird. 

00:04:53.005 --> 00:04:56.889
She hoped he was enjoying the skies — just like that.

00:04:58.661 --> 00:05:02.439
And every time the bird saw a whale 
diving deep in the ocean,

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:05.141
he thought of his whale.

00:05:05.904 --> 00:05:08.472
He hoped she was enjoying the ocean —

00:05:08.481 --> 00:05:11.015
— just like that.

